<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-AutoZone estimates raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-AutoZone estimates raised.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- EVEREN Securities Inc said Wednesday it increased its 1997 earnings estimate for AutoZone Inc to $1.30 from $1.28 and the estimate for 1998 to $1.60 from $1.55.</p>
<p>-- EVEREN also raised its price targets to $30 from $26 for the near term and to $32 from $28 for the long term.</p>
<p>-- The upgrade was based on attractive valuation and better-than-expected commercial installer business rollout, EVEREN said. AutoZone is also expanding into new markets, which will help same-store comparisons, EVEREN said.</p>
<p>-- AutoZone markets auto parts.</p>
<p>-- Its shares were off 1/8 Wednesday at 26.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
